# Files and directories Vercel should NOT upload during deploy.
#
# This file is carried into the brand-deploy mirror by sync-vercel.yml
# (it copies the whole services/command-center/ tree to a tmpdir and
# pushes from there). Vercel reads .vercelignore at the root of that
# pushed tree and skips matching paths.
#
# Goal: keep the deploy upload lean. Vercel rebuilds dependencies +
# Next output anyway, so node_modules/.next/.turbo are pure noise.
# Dev-only docs (CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md/.claude/) help local agents but
# nothing in the deployed app reads them.

# Build outputs — Vercel regenerates these from package.json + source
node_modules/
.next/
.turbo/

# Local environment files (Vercel uses dashboard env vars + env pulls)
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Dev tooling that lives alongside source — claude-code agent definitions,
# editor metadata, MCP configs. None of it ships to runtime.
.claude/
.cursor/
.vscode/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
.mcp.json

# Brand prebuild moves the active brand's pack into public/brand/ at
# build time. Vercel runs `npm run build` which triggers brand-prebuild,
# so the source packs/configs need to ship — DO NOT add branding/ here.
